  "context": "Related done item perf-questdb-influxdb-load-20261030. Pre-existing. Not fixed by the verifier.\n\nFixed in PR #3981 (merge c1a2dc186b). Verdict: PRE-EXISTING (7aa4a8b391, before #3952, loads lineitem as 0 rows with SUCCESS). Before (head, after the socket fix): lineitem 0 rows, load now FAILED loudly (Broken pipe from QuestDB rejecting STRING->TIMESTAMP lines). After: column types from SHOW COLUMNS, date columns sent as epoch-micros timestamps; lineitem 60175 rows and all 8 tables at source counts; l_shipdate, l_commitdate, l_receiptdate equal the file for all 60175 rows. Unparseable dates now raise instead of taking server time.",
  "description": "Found by live verification of #3952 (perf-questdb-influxdb-load-20261030) on origin/develop 525361b2f8, questdb/questdb:10.0.1, loading_method=ilp, TPC-H SF0.01.\n\nExpected: lineitem loads 60175 rows (l_shipdate designated timestamp, l_commitdate and l_receiptdate as timestamps).\nActual: lineitem has 0 rows and the load reports SUCCESS. QuestDB log: `LineWalAppender could not write line protocol measurement [tableName=lineitem ... column: l_commitdate; cast error from protocol type: STRING to column type: TIMESTAMP`. The ILP builder (_ilp_lines_from_strings in benchbox/platforms/questdb.py) converts only the designated column from TPCH_TIMESTAMP_COLUMNS to epoch nanoseconds; every other date column is quoted as a string, and QuestDB rejects the line and drops the connection. Same on the pre-#3952 commit 7aa4a8b391 (0 rows), so not a regression. Logs /tmp/live-verify-questdb-check.log, /tmp/live-verify-questdb-check-base3952.log, /tmp/live-verify-questdb-load.log.\n\nSuspected: _ilp_lines_from_strings / _ilp_field_values (need per-column type awareness from SHOW COLUMNS, emitting timestamp columns as `<epoch_micros>t` or nanosecond integers).",
